hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4786","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabab, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: “The child born of adultery will not enter Paradise, nor the second, nor the third.”"
"4787","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The child of adultery is the worst of the three.”"
"4788","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Sulaiman told us, saying: I heard Ibn Wahb, saying: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and another mentioned Before that, on the authority of Bukayr, he heard Kurayb say: I heard Maymunah bint Al-Harith say: “I freed a female child in the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” peace be upon him, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: If you had given to your maternal uncles, your reward would have been greater.” Muhammad disagreed with him. Ibn Ishaq (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4789",""
"4790","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Al-Hilalia that was at The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that she had a black slave girl, and she said: O Messenger of God, “I wanted to free this woman. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Will you not ransom your brother’s daughter or your sister’s daughter by herding sheep?”"
"4791","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Muhammad bin Khazim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, on the authority of Maimuna, that she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a servant, and he gave her A servant, so I freed her. He said: What did you do to the servant? She said: O Messenger of God, I freed her. He said: If you had given her to your maternal uncles, your reward would have been greater. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4792","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, he said: I am Zuhayr, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr. On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that she said: O Prophet of God, “I wanted to free this boy. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Rather, give it to your brother who is a Bedouin who is being looked after, for he is greater for your reward. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4793","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Mawhib told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, He said: And Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Hammad bin Masada. He said: Ibn Mawhib told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: It was Aisha has a husband and a boy and a slave girl. She said: So I wanted to emancipate them, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Start with the boy before the girl.” Muhammad bin Bashar said in his hadith, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you free them, then start.” “With the man before the woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4794","Ahmad bin Abdul-Wahid told us, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, and he mentioned another before him, they said: Ubayd Allah bin Abi Jafar told us, On the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr bin Umayyah Al-Damri, that he narrated to him that men from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to him that the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Any female slave who is under a slave and is freed, she has the choice as long as her husband does not have intercourse with her.”"
"4795","Hannad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Abu Lahwas, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a portion of a slave belonging to him shall guarantee to his companions their inheritance.”"
"4796","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Husayn bin Ayyash told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’ told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, And Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Umar, I said: On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, he said: “Whoever frees a freed woman in which there is shirk, then the completion of his emancipation depends on the one who freed him.” On the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Adhrami , on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of sheikhs from the people of Mecca, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, In the same way (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4797","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Daoud bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Amr bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Whoever has a slave between himself and another, and frees his share, then he will stand up against him and free him.”"
"4798","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ If a slave is between two people, and one of them frees his share, then if he is well-off, a value is assessed on him, no compensation or excess, then he is freed. \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4799","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, that he heard Salim bin Abdullah bin Omar, speaking on the authority of Ibn Omar, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If a servant is between two people, and one of them frees his share, then if he is affluent, it is only He owes a just price, no loss or excess, so he will give it to its owner and set him free.”"
"4800","4800 Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever frees a partner of his in a slave will complete what remains in his property, if he has property equal to the price of the slave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4801","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever frees a share in a property, what remains of his wealth will be established.” Al-Zuhri said: If he has wealth equal to its price."
"4802","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar Al-Basri told us, he said: I am Suwayd, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees any of a property, must free it all if he has property equal to its price.” If he does not have any wealth, his share of it will be freed.”"
"4803","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Khalaf bin Tamim narrated to us, he said: Zaydah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a share in a slave has freed all of it, if the one who freed his share of the money equals its price.” A fair value will be assessed on his wealth, and if he does not have any wealth, then what he has freed will be freed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4804","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever has polytheism in a slave and frees him, then he has been freed, if he has money upon which a value can be established.” He is just with his wealth, and if he does not have any wealth, then he frees from it what he frees.”"
"4805","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said He said: “Whoever frees a partner of his in a slave, he frees all of him. If the one who freed his share of the money equals its price, then he must free him.” He said: This is what Yahya said without a doubt (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4806","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: I am Yahya, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever frees a partner of his in a property, he has been freed. If he has money equal to its price, then he will be freed from his wealth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4807","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: I am human, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a partner of his in a slave, he has freed all of him, if the one who freed his share of the money equals its price, a fair value will be assessed on it. Then he will give to his partners their relatives, and his way will be cleared.”"
"4808","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: I am Muhammad bin Salamah, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Zaid told me, on the authority of Omar bin Nafi’ And Ubayd Allah bin Umar, and Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Whenever a man has a share in a slave, and he frees his share of him and has wealth equal to the value of the shares of his partners, he is guaranteed “His associates will have their kinsfolk, and He will free the slave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4809","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Any property owned by partners, and one of them frees his share, then a fair value will be applied to the property of the one who freed him, and he will be freed if it reaches \"That's his money.\""
"4810","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, then he mentioned a word that means: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar. The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever frees his share in a property and has money equal to its price, he must He will set him free in its entirety.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4811","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever frees a shareholder in a property, and has money equal to its price at fair value, then he will be freed from his wealth.”"
"4812","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Wahhab Al-Thaqafi, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever frees a share in a property, and has money equivalent to its price at fair value, then he is freed, and perhaps He said: “And if he has no money, then he frees what he freed.” And perhaps he did not say it, and my greatest suspicion is that it is something he says that is beneficial on his part. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4813","Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ Whoever freed a share of his, or he said: a share, or he said: a share of his in a slave, and he had money equal to its price at a fair value, He is freed, otherwise he has freed what he has freed.” Ayoub said: Perhaps Nafi’ said this in the hadith, and perhaps he did not say it, so I do not know whether he said it in the hadith. Is the hadith said, or is it beneficial before him, meaning: His saying: He freed from it what was freed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4814","Al-Harith bin Miskin, I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a share of his in a slave and has wealth equal to the price of the slave, then judge him.” “The value of the slave, so his partners were given their shares and the slave was freed. Otherwise, whatever of him was freed will be freed.”"
"4815","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, he told him that Abdullah bin Omar He used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a share in a person is responsible for freeing what remains. If he has no money, then he He rewarded what he did.”"
"4816","Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a share of a human being is his duty to free what remains.” Nafi’ said: If it is not what he frees, then what he frees is permissible. made"
"4817","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed, saying: I heard Nafi’ speaking, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever frees his share in a owned property, he will be responsible for what is left and free it,” and it was Nafi’ says: Yahya said: I do not know whether it was something he said before, or something in the hadith: If he did not have it, then what he did is permissible."
"4818","On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Nafi’, on the authority of Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Yunus bin Abd, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “Whoever frees a shaqis in a slaveholding, if he has wealth, we will appoint it over him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4819","4818 Amr bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Hafs, who is Ibn Ghailan, on the authority of Sulayman bin Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever frees a slave and he has partners in him, and he has loyalty, is free. He guarantees the share of his partners in value, because of the wrongdoing of his sharing with them, and the servant does not owe anything.”"
"4820","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a share of his in a property, his redemption from him is in his property, if he has any property. “He did not have any money. That servant was assessed its fair value, and he sought its value for its owner, without making any payment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4821","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever frees someone of his own in a kingdom, he must free him in His money if he has money, otherwise give the property a fair value, so make an effort without being too harsh on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4822","Al-Mu'mal ibn Hisham Al-Basri informed us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Sa'id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashir ibn It is forbidden, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever frees someone who is in need of a slave, his salvation will be from his wealth, if he has any wealth. If he does not have any money, the servant can run without any hardship on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4823","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Qatada told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Anas, On the authority of Bashir ibn Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a part of his own in a slave, it is upon him That he frees the rest of him if he has money, otherwise the servant should run without any hardship on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4824","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “In the property owned between two men, one of them frees his share,” he said: He guarantees (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4825","4824 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Amir, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever frees his share in a property will be freed from his wealth, if he has any.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4826","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a poor slave from a slave will be freed from his wealth, if he has any.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4827","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ibn al-Talib, On the authority of his father, that a man “emancipated his share in a property, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not guarantee it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4828","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada told us, and Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: we told him Hibban, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, that a man from Hudhayl “freed a shaqays from a Mamluk, so he permitted The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, freed him and said: “God has no partner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4829","Al-Mu'mal bin Hisham told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Sa'id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, that a man \"freed a friend of his from... A slave, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made his allowance from his wealth, and said: “There is no partner with God.”"
"4830","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Amir told me, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, that a man “emancipated He was a slave among Mamluk, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He was freed from his wealth if he had any, and he said: And God has no partner. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4831","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Amr ibn Aoun told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu Zaid, that A man from the Ansar freed six slaves upon his death, and he had no property other than them. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided them into three parts. So he freed two, and enslaved four, and said: If I had witnessed him before he was buried, he would not have been buried in the Muslim graves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4832","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that A man from the Ansar “manumitted six slaves upon his death, and he had no wealth other than them. Then the news reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said about it: He spoke harshly, then he summoned them and distributed them, then he cast lots among them and freed two, and enslaved four.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4833","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Hushaym, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man “emancipated six slaves.” When he died, he had no wealth other than them, so this reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he became angry about that, and said: I thought that I will not pray for him. Then he summoned his Mamluks and divided them into three parts, then he cast lots among them, freeing two and enslaving four.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4834","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ informed us, saying: Yazid told us, Yunus told us: on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man “was freed.” Six slaves. He had no property other than them, so he freed them upon his death. They were brought to the attention of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he disliked that. Then He divided them into three parts and cast lots among them, freeing two and enslaving four.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4835","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, Qatada, Humaid, and Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man “emancipated six slaves.” When he died, he had no property other than them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cast lots among them, and he freed two, and returned four to slavery. \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4836","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran told us, he said: Bishr told us, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Awf told us, and Muhammad bin Sirin said, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “A man of the Muslims during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and he left behind six slaves, and that he freed them.” At the time of death of all of them, and he did not leave anyone else’s wealth, so it was presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cast lots. among them, so he freed two and enslaved four.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4837","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mukhtar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man “emancipated six of his slaves upon his death, and he had no property other than them, at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Peace be upon him, so he divided them into parts, freeing two and enslaving four.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4838","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Ashhab, he said: Al-Layth informed me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja`far, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a slave and has wealth, the slave’s wealth is his, unless “The master stipulates, and it is his.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4839","4838 Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Abdul Wahhab bin Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam informed us, he said: Tell me Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Al-Layth, and another mentioned, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ja’far, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever frees a slave and has wealth, his wealth is his, unless the master makes an exception.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4840","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id speaking, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Any man who sells a date-palm tree has had its fruit ripened, so its fruit is the first to go.” And any man who sells a property and has money, his money belongs to its first owner, unless the buyer stipulates it.” Shu’bah said: So I told him the hadith of Ayyub. On the authority of Nafi’, that he told me about palm trees, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Mamluk on the authority of Omar, so Abd Rabb said: I do not know them all except On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he said again, and he narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had no doubt. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4841","4840 Amr bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Hafs, who is Ibn Ghaylan, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Ataa, and on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells a slave while he has money, gets his money, unless he stipulates The purchaser, and whoever plants a palm tree that he sells after planting it, gets its fruit, unless the purchaser stipulates.”"
"4842","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Ata’, and Ibn Abi Mulaika, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys a fruited palm tree, its fruit belongs to the seller, unless the purchaser stipulates, and whoever sells a slave He has money, and his money belongs to his master, unless the buyer stipulates it.”"
"4843","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “A lifetime spent a slave being sold and he had money. His money belongs to his master who sold him, unless the buyer stipulates that his money be his.”"
"4844","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, and he said another time, Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar. On the authority of Omar, he said: “Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it.”"
"4845","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar said: “Whoever sells a slave and has money “Then his money goes to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it.”"
"4846","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told me, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, that Umar “decided on the property of the slave to his master, except That the buyer stipulates (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4847","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, he said: My father told me, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, On the authority of Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever buys a fruited palm tree, its fruit will go to the first seller, unless the buyer stipulates “And whoever sells a slave while he has money, his money goes to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4848","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, my father told me, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, and whoever He sells a palm tree that has been ripened and its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it.”"
"4849","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ Whoever buys a palm tree after it has been pollinated, its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, and whoever sells a slave and he has money, his money is for the seller, unless That the buyer stipulates that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4850","Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Rafi’ informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, who said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells a slave, his property belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, and whoever sells palm trees In it there is fruit that has been ripened, so its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, and the wording is attributed to Muhammad. Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: we told us. Muammar, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, like this hadith of al-Zuhri And Ishaq said the same thing (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4851","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: Thani my father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever sells a slave while he has money,” he mentioned something like the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4852","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Warith told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jumhan, on the authority of a ship, he said: I was owned by Umm Salamah. She said: “I free you, and I stipulate that you serve the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as long as you live.” So I said: If you do not stipulate that I will not leave the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him as long as I lived, so she freed me and made a stipulation of me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4853","Muhammad bin Uthman told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammad told us, on his authority, and Muhammad bin Uthman told us, he said: Bahz told us, Hammad told us Bin Salamah, he said: Saeed bin Jumhan told us, on the authority of Safina, he said: “Umm Salamah freed me, and stipulated that I should serve the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he was safe as long as he lived.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4854","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I heard Jabir, “on the authority of a man from his people, that “He freed a slave after a while, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him and sold him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4855","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, that a man “manumitted a slave of his for He returned, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him and sold him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4856","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ghandar told us, he said: The teacher, meaning Husayn, told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd. By God, a man freed a slave of his own, and the man was in need, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who will buy him? So he bought him. Nuaym bin Abdullah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took its price and gave it to him.”"
"4857","4856 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Thana Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abdul Majeed bin Suhail, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that a man from the Ansar freed a slave of his who was in need, and he was in need. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he called him and said: Have you freed your servant? He said: Yes. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you have more need of him? Then he said: Who will buy him? Nuaym bin Abdullah: I did. So he bought it, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took its price and gave it to its owner. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4858","Mahmoud bin Khalid Al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ata’ narrated to us, that Jabir narrated to him, saying: “A man was appointed to The time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. A servant of his who had no other property was freed after him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took He sold the slave, then gave his owner his price.”"
"4859","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan and Ibn Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sold the one who managed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4860","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He freed a slave of his after a while, and he did not have He sold someone else’s money, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sold it for eight hundred dirhams and gave it to his master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4861","Abu Dawud told us, he said: A lecturer told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “A man was freed from The Ansar had a servant of his who had left behind, and he was in need and had a debt, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sold him for eight hundred dirhams. So he gave it to him and said: “Pay off your debt.”"
"4862","4861 Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that a man freed a slave of his who had died, and his master was in need, so he ordered him to be sold, so he sold him for eight hundred, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him: “Spend it on your children, for charity is only given out of wealth, and start with those you support.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4863","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ismail told us, he said: I am Ayyub, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that a man from the Ansar was called: Abu Mathkur said, “He freed a slave of his who was called Ya’qub. He had no one else, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him and said: Who will buy it? Who will buy it? So Nu`aym bin Abdullah bought it for eight hundred dirhams, so he sent it to him and said: If it is one of you. A poor person, let him start with himself, and if he is benevolent, then on his dependents, and if there is benevolence, then on his relatives, or on his relatives, if \"There is virtue here and there.\""
"4864","4863 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he said: “A man from Banu ‘Uthrah freed a slave He had some money, and that was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you have any wealth other than that? He said: No, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: Who will buy it from me? So Nu`aym bin Abdullah Al-Adawi bought it for eight hundred dirhams, and he brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted him and handed it to him, then said: Start with yourself and give it in charity. If there is anything left over, then it is for your family. If there is anything left over for your family, then for it. Your kinship, and if there is anything left over from your kinship, then this and that.” He says: “Before your hands, on your right, and on your left.”"
"4865","Abdullah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father and my uncle told us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir Bin Abdullah, that a man “emancipated a slave of his who had no other property, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned him to him, and Nu’aym bought him \"Bin Al-Nahham\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4866","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd, he said: “ His son slapped a servant of his, and he said to him: “Smite him.” He said: He let him go. Then he said: We had a mamluk, Banu Muqrin, and a man from among us slapped him. So he complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was told: He has no one else, so he said: Either no, let him serve them until they can do without him."
"4867","Ahmad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Asbat, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abul-Safar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd bin Muqrin, “The Banu Muqrin had a boy Some of us slapped him, then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and complained to him. He freed him, and it was said: O Messenger of God, he has no servant other than himself. He said: To serve them until they no longer need him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4868","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd, he said: “I slapped a servant of ours.” So my father said: Take retaliation, then he said: We were seven Banu Muqrin, and we had no servant except one, so one of us slapped her, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “Free her.” It was said: “They have no servant other than her.” He said: “If they have no need of her, then let them free her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4869","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir told me: What is your name? I said: Shu’bah. He said: Abu Shu’bah told me, and he was kind. He said: I witnessed Suwayd bin Muqrin, and a man slapped a boy. He said: “Did you not know The surah is forbidden. You saw that I was the seventh of seven brothers at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. We only had one boy, so he slapped him. One of us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to free him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4870","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, he said: We used to sell linen in Suwayd bin Muqrin went home, and a maid came out and said something to one of our men, and he slapped her. Suwayd got angry and said: Did you slap her face? ! “I saw that I was the seventh of seven of my brothers with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We had no servant except one, and one of us slapped her. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to free her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4871","4870 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Al-Layth informed me, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There are three rights that God has a duty to help: the one who seeks to fulfill his duties, and the one who marries him.” He desires chastity, and strives in the cause of God.”"
"4872","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Barirah wrote on It is nine uqiyahs by itself, an uqiyah every year, so Aisha came to ask for help, and she said: No, unless they want that I prepare it for them in a number. One, and allegiance will be to me. So Bareerah went and spoke about this to her family, but they refused to give her anything except that allegiance be to them, so she came. To Aisha, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came at that time, and she said to her: What did her family say? She said: No, by God, then, unless the loyalty is to me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is this? I said: O Messenger of God! “Barira came to me seeking my help in writing it, so I said: No, unless they want me to count it as one number, and the loyalty is to me. So she mentioned that to her family, but they refused to give her anything except that allegiance be to them. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Buy her. And he stipulated their loyalty, for loyalty belongs to the one who is freed. Then he got up and addressed the people, thanking God and praising Him, then he said: What is the matter with people? They stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of God. They say: I free so-and-so and his loyalty is to me. The Book of God is more worthy, and the condition of God is more reliable, and every condition is not in the Book. By God, it is invalid, and if it were one hundred conditions, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a choice from her husband - and he was a slave, so she chose herself.” Urwah said: If he had been free, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not have given her a choice."
"4873","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Men of knowledge told me, including: Yunus bin Yazid, And Al-Layth bin Saad, that Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, She said: “Barira came to me and said: O Aisha, I have written to my family for nine uqiyas, an uqiya every year, so help me. She had not completed anything of what she had written, so Aisha said to her, and sighed over it: Go back to your family, if they would like me to give them that. All of you, and your loyalty will be to me. I did so, so Barirah went to her family and proposed this to them, but they refused and said: If she wishes, It is expected of you, so do it, and your loyalty will be to us. So Aisha mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: He will not prevent you. That is one of them, buy me and free me, for loyalty is to the one who frees me, so I did, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up among the people and praised God. He praised him, then said: What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of God? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of God is invalid, even if “There were a hundred conditions. God’s decree is more valid, and God’s condition is more reliable. Loyalty is only to the one who is freed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4874","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Al-Thaqafi told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, sixty years ago, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Barira, she said: There were three Sunnah rituals: She gave me meat as charity, so I gave it to Aisha, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered. He said: “What is this meat?” She said: “Meat that you give as charity to Bareerah, so she gave it to us.” He said: “It is charity given to Barira and we give it as a gift.” She wrote for nine times, and Aisha said: If your masters wish, I can count for them your price in one number, so she said: They say: Except that “You stipulate loyalty for them, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Buy it and stipulate for them, for loyalty belongs to the one who is freed.” She said: He freed me, so I had the choice. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4875","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I learned it from Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that Bareerah came To Aisha, asking her about her writing, and her family said: If you wish, you can give the rest of her writing, and we will have loyalty. So when the Prophet came May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I mentioned that to him, and he said: Buy her and free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees her. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went up. The pulpit, peace be upon him, said: What is the matter with people stipulating conditions that are not in the Book of God? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of God, it is not permissible for him. And if he stipulated one hundred conditions, (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4876","Suleiman bin Salam Al-Balkhi told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr, he said: I am Hisham, and Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, He said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The one who has been freed must pay the blood money of a freeman according to what he has freed, and according to the amount of blood money he has freed from the slave.”"
"4877","Ubayd Allah bin Faddalah Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He decreed in the offices that he should pay according to what he was freed from.”"
"4878","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If he receives a share or an inheritance, he inherits on account of what he has freed, and it is established upon him.” “The punishment is on account of what he has freed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4879","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ali, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “He fulfills what is requested according to what he fulfilled.” Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: we told him. Ismail bin Ulayya, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ali, similar to him, but he did not narrate it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4880","Abu Bakr bin Ali Al-Maruzi told me, he said: Ubayd Allah Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, that “ He was killed during the reign of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had paid a group of people. So he ordered that what he had paid be paid the blood money of a free man, and what was the blood money of a slave. \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4881","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ali, he said: “If he pays half, then he is a debtor.”"
"4882","Amr bin Zurarah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: I am Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any servant who is appointed for one hundred uqiyahs, he pays it except ten uqiyahs, then completes"
"4883","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ Al-Jariri, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Any slave who writes for one hundred dinars and pays it for nothing less than ten dinars is a slave. And any slave who is debited for one hundred waqiyyas and pays for it except ten waqiyyas, then he is a slave.” Al-Alaa Al-Jariri said this."
"4884","On the authority of Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Amr ibn Asim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Abbas al-Jariri, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Any slave who wrote down a hundred uqiyahs and paid for it except ten.” Awaq, then he is a slave, and any slave who wrote down for one hundred dinars and paid for it minus ten dinars, then he is a slave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4885","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ataa told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: O Messenger of God! “We hear hadiths from you. Do you give us permission to write them down?” He said: “Yes.” It was the first thing that was written, the letter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. To the people of Mecca: Two conditions are not permissible in a single sale, nor a combined sale and credit, nor a sale that is not guaranteed, or a sale of one hundred dirhams. If he spends it on the sum of ten dirhams, then he is a slave, or if he spends it on a hundred uqiyahs, except two uqiyas, then he is a slave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4886","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad al-Harrani told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Yazid al-Harrani told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman. Mawla of the Talha family, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There was a representative of Umm Salamah called: Nabhan. Umm Salamah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he says: “If the person being sought finds something that leads to it, hide from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4887","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr Al-Jahdhami told us, he said: We are Abdul-Ala, Muammar said: On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Nabhan, on the authority of Umm Salamah, She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “If the person being sought finds something to lead, then hide from him.”"
"4888","Muhammad bin Nasr told me, he said: Ayoub bin Sulaiman told me, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais told me, on the authority of Sulayman bin Bilal, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Atiq, and Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Nabhan, the offices of Umm Salamah, that Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to us: “If there is something in the office of one of you that you are required to write, then hide from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4889","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin told me Muslim Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Nabhan, the client of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “covenanted to us: If When one of you writes, meaning: in fulfillment of what remains of his writing, so veil yourself from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4890","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, in the hadith of Nabhan, Umm said: Salamah: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If there is something to be done by someone who is appointed, then hide from him.”"
"4891","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us again, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Nabhan, the servant of Umm Salamah, told him that Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had made a covenant with us, if “One of us has offices, so he completed what remained of his writing, so set aside the veil.”"
"4892","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us. He said: I am Abdul Razzaq. He said: I am Ibn Jurayj. He said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told me that Abdullah bin Habib told him, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “And give them of the wealth of God which He has given you.” He said: A quarter of what is required. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4893","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, On the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “And give them of the wealth of God that He has given you.” He said: “A quarter of the reward.” Ibn Juraij said: And he told me More than one person, on the authority of Ata’, that he used to narrate this hadith without mentioning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4894","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: “ And give them of the wealth of God which He has given you.” He said: “A quarter of the reward.”"
"4895","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Abd al-Malik, and he is the son of Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Ayan, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, that he wrote down a servant of his for four thousand, then he assigned a thousand on his behalf, and then said: “Had I not seen Ali writing As a servant of his, then he compensated for a quarter of what I did.”"
"4896","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Makki bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir, He says: “We used to sell our concubines to the mothers of children, while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was alive. We saw no harm in that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4897","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “We used to sell mothers of Children at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we do not deny that.”"
"4898","4896 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, “ Regarding the mothers of children, he said: We used to sell them at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Zayd the blind is not With the strong (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4899","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi told us, he said: I am Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abdullah bin Muhairiz informed me Al-Jumahi, that Abu Saeed told him that: While he was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from the Ansar came and said: Oh The Messenger of God, “We are the share of captives and we love precious things, so how do you think about isolation?” The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Or will you do that? “No, you should not do that, for it is not a breeze. God has decreed that it should go out, but it will go out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4900","Harun bin Saeed bin Al-Haytham Al-Ayli told us, he said: Khalid bin Nizar told me, he said: Al-Qasim bin Mabrur told me, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, Ibn Shihab said: Abdullah bin Muhayriz told me that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri told him that: While he was sitting at The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from the Ansar said: O Messenger of God, “We are taking captives, and we love pricey things. So what do you think about Isolation? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Or do you not do that? To go out unless she is going out.”"
"4901","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail bin Jafar told us, he said: Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz He said: Abu Sarmah and I entered upon Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, and Abu Sarmah asked him, and he said: O Abu Sa`id, did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? “Does he mention the defenseless?” He said: “Yes, we invaded with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the battle of the Banu al-Mustaliq, and they took us as noble captives.” Arabs. Singleness became too long for us, and we desired women. We wanted to enjoy ourselves and be alone, so we said: We will do so, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace We did not ask him, may God bless him and grant him peace, before us. So we asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You do not have to do what God has ordained for creation. A breath that exists until the Day of Resurrection, but it will exist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4902","Abdul Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told me, on the authority of Rabia bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, he said: Abu Sarmah and I entered upon Abu Sa`id. Al-Khudri, so we asked him “about isolation,” and Abu Sa’id said: “We captured the women of Banu Mutaliq and we wanted to isolate them,” so some of us said to each other: Are you isolated while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is among you and you do not ask him? So we said: O Messenger of God, we have captured the noblemen of the Arabs. We have captured the women of Banu. Al-Muslim, and we wanted to be isolated, and we wanted to make a ransom. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You do not have to do it, for it is what “From a breath that God has decreed that it should exist until the Day of Resurrection except that it exists,” Abd al-Malik ibn Shuaib ibn al-Layth informed us, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, Ibn Ayyub said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Muhayriz, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4903","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of his brother Ma’bad bin Sirin, he said: I told Abu Saeed Al-Khudri: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about isolation? He said: Yes, we asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about isolation, and he said: What is it? So we said: A man has a wife. The breastfeeding woman hates for her to become pregnant, so he is separated from her. Or he has a slave girl who has no property other than her, so he may be affected by her, so he hates to She became pregnant and he was cut off from her. He said: No, you should not do that, for it is destiny. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4904","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Harun, he said: I am Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr. He transmitted the hadith to Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, and said: We said: O Messenger of God, “A man has a breastfeeding woman with him, and he gets infected from her.” He hates for her to become pregnant, and he has a slave girl with him, so he may have sexual intercourse with her, and he hates for her to become pregnant, so he should be separated from her. He said: Should you not? “You do so, for it is decree.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4905","Remembrance of God. Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Saif told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Maysarah, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: “When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, Omar said: “O God, give us a satisfactory explanation regarding alcohol. Then the verse concerning Al-Baqarah was revealed, and Omar was called and it was read to him. Omar said: O God, give us a satisfactory explanation regarding wine, so the verse concerning wine was revealed. Women: O you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are drunk until you know what you are saying. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was calling When he established the prayer, he would call out: Do not approach the prayer while you are drunk until you know what you are saying. So Omar was called and it was read to him, and he said: Oh God, make it clear for us. Concerning wine, a satisfactory explanation, so the verse on the table was revealed, so Omar was called and it was read to him, and when he reached the age of, “Have you finished?” Omar said May God be pleased with him: We are finished, we are finished."
"4906","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, informed us, on the authority of Sulaiman Al-Taymi, that Anas bin Malik told them He said: “While I was standing in charge of the neighborhood, and I was the youngest of them in age, a man came and said: Wine has been forbidden, and I was standing.” It is upon them to give me something to give them to drink from what was abundant for them. They said: Enough of it. So I said to Anas: What is it? He said: Al-Busr and dates. Abu Bakr said. Ibn Anas: Their wine was that day, but Anas did not deny it."
"4907","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “ I was giving water to Abu Talha, Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and Abu Dujana with a group of the Ansar, when a man entered and said: There has been news. The prohibition of wine, so that was enough for it. He said: On that day, it was nothing but fadhikh, a mixture of walnuts and dates. He said: And Anas said: You have forbidden wine. And most of their wines on that Day will be abundant.”"
"4908","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Humaid al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Alcohol was forbidden when it was forbidden, and that “For their drink is dried fruits and dates.”"
"4909","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, he said: I heard on the authority of Jabir bin Abdul God says: “Cuts and dates are wine.”"
"4910","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah informed us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Raisins and dates are wine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4911","Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, saying: Abd al-Rahman informed us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of a man from The Companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade dates and dates, raisins and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4912","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of dried fruits, hantams, tamzafats, and niqir, and mixing dates with And arrogance"
"4913","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Amra, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of dried dates and raisins, and he added again: and naqir, and to mix dates with raisins. And taking pride in dates.”"
"4914","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Artat, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the eating of fresh fruits and dates, and raisins and dates.”"
"4915","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: he told me Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not combine dates with raisins, nor combine vanity. And the wet one (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4916","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Ali, who is Ibn Al-Mubarak, told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not reject fresh and fresh dates altogether, and do not reject raisins.” And all the wet ones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4917","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Saeed, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade mixing dates and raisins, and mixing zhou And dates, and pride and beauty.”"
"4918","Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He forbade the mixture of dates and raisins, and dates and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4919","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Bastam told us, he said: Malik bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not mix raisins and dates, or walnuts and dates.”"
"4920","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that: “ He forbade raisins and dates to be rejected altogether, and he forbade all cranberries and dates to be rejected.”"
"4921","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala informed us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the lizard, the hantam, the zifat, the naqir, and the Whole grains and dates are not to be mixed, and raisins and dates are to be mixed, and He wrote to the people of Hijra: “Do not mix raisins and dates together.”"
"4922","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Alone is forbidden, and with dates is forbidden.”"
"4923","Muhammad bin Adam and Ali bin Saeed told us, saying: Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the mixture of dates and raisins, and the mixing of dates and raisins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4924","Quraysh bin Abdul Rahman informed us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hasan, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid informed us, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me, He said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah saying: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade whole grains and raisins, and he forbade whole grains and dates.” to mix all together with wine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4925","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not give up fresh dates and dates, and do not give up dates and raisins altogether.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4926","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that: “ He forbade the rejection of raisins and whole grains, and he forbade the rejection of whole wheat and fresh dates.”"
"4927","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Waqa’ bin Iyas, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Fulfil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us from combining two things, wine, of which one of them would be offensive to its owner. He said: And I asked him about the foul.” So he forbade me from him, saying: “And he hated the common sinner for fear that they might be two things, so we used to cut him off.”"
"4928","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Abu Idris, he said: “I witnessed Anas bin Malik A guilty camel was brought and he began to cut it off.”"
"4929","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that he used to: “He does not leave anything that has become wet without removing it.” \"about his eloquence\""
"4930","Suwayd ibn Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Arouba, Qatada said: Anas used to command people to commit sins. Then it will be lent.”"
"4931","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of Abi Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not abandon the arrogant and the wet altogether, nor the And raisins all together, and reject each one of them separately.”"
"4932","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Abu Ismail told us, he said: Yahya told us, that Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told him, On the authority of his father, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade the mixture of jujubes and dates, and the mixture of raisins and dates, and said: Reject each one.” “Some of them are placed separately in the waters on the mouths of which the stone is smeared.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4933","4933 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim Al-Abdi, he said: Abu Al-Mutawakkil told us, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us “to mix cranberries with dates, or raisins with dates, or Raisins with basur. He said: Whoever of you drinks it, let each one drink from it individually, or raisins individually, or raisins individually, or raisins individually.”"
"4934","Ahmad bin Khalid told me, he said: Shuaib bin Harb told us, he said: Ismail bin Muslim told us, he said: Abu Al-Mutawakkil told us Al-Naji, said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade mixing walnuts with dates or raisins.” with dates, or raisins with large seeds, and said: Whoever of you drinks, let each one of you drink of it individually.”"
"4935","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, he said: Abu Kathir told us He said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “mixing dates and raisins, and dates and dates, and dates and raisins.” And dates, and he said: Discard each one of them separately."
"4936","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told us, saying: Al-Mu’afāf, meaning Ibn Imran, told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil On the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade the rejection of dates and raisins, and of dates and dates, and he said: Avoid raisins alone. “And the dates individually, and the raw dates alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4937","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Kathir told me, and his name is Yazid bin Abdul. The Most Gracious, and Humayd bin Masada told us, saying: Sufyan is Ibn Habib told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Kathir told us, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Wine is from.” Suwayd said: In these two trees: the palm tree. And the grape"
"4938","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Hajjaj al-Sawwaf told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Kathir told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The wine is from these two trees: the palm tree.” And the grape"
"4939","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, he said: Al-Sha’bi told us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: I heard Omar, may God be pleased with him, delivering a sermon on the pulpit of Medina, and he said: O people, the prohibition of alcohol was revealed on the day it was revealed while it was Of five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, barley, and wine, whatever the mind is dulled with.”"
"4940","4944 Muhammad ibn Al-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Idris informed us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard Umar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, on the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “As for what follows, the prohibition on alcohol was revealed, and it is one of the Five: grapes, wheat, barley, dates, and honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4941","4945 Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “ Wine is made from five things: dates, wheat, barley, honey, and grapes.”"
"4942","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: A man came to Ibn Omar, and he said: “ Our family would arrange for us to drink in the evening, so when we drank in the morning, he said: He forbade intoxicants, both small and large, and I bear witness. May God bless you, the people of Khaybar prefer such-and-such a drink, and they call it such-and-such, which is wine, and the people of Fadak They choose a drink from such-and-such, and they call it such-and-such, and it is wine, until he enumerated four drinks, one of which is honey.”"
"4943","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’. On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is alcohol.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4944","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden. And every intoxicant is wine.” Al-Hussein bin Mansour said: Ahmad bin Hanbal said: This is an authentic hadith."
"4945","Yahya bin Darust told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Every intoxicant is wine.”"
"4946","Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Rawad told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is alcohol, and every intoxicant is forbidden.”"
"4947","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is alcohol.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4948","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4949","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4950","4954 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “He forbade the use of ṣaba’, ṣaffat, niqīr, and hantam, and every intoxicant is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
